#: ../../api.md:27
msgid "Verification core"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core:1
msgid "Sans-I/O verification core."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core:3
msgid ""
":func:`verification_steps` is a generator that yields :data:`Effect` "
"requests (DNS / HTTPS lookups) and receives their results via ``send``.  "
"Drivers in :mod:`pyevp.verifier` run it synchronously or asynchronously; "
"tests can drive it by hand.  Everything else in this module is a pure "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.FetchJson:1
msgid "Request the JSON document at ``url``.  Reply with the decoded JSON value."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.FetchJson:3
msgid "``refresh`` asks the driver to bypass its cache (e.g. after key rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.MarkUsed:1
msgid ""
"Record that a token has been accepted.  Reply ``True`` if it was not seen"
" before."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.MarkUsed:3
msgid ""
"``key`` only needs remembering until ``expires_at``: from that instant "
"on, the token fails the freshness checks anyway.  Freshness is judged "
"once, before any I/O, so a driver must reject the token "
"(``TOKEN_EXPIRED``) if its clock has reached ``expires_at`` after "
"marking: the record may already be gone, and a replay would not find it."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.ResolveTxt:1
msgid ""
"Request the TXT records of ``name``.  Reply with ``list[str]`` (empty if "
"none)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.precheck_evt:1
msgid "Check everything about the EVT that does not need the issuer's keys."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.replay_key:1
msgid "Stable identifier of a presentation for replay detection."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.replay_key:3
msgid ""
"It is derived from the KB-JWT signing input (header and payload), not "
"from the whole token: signatures can be re-encoded without the holder key"
" (ECDSA ``s`` → ``n - s``, non-canonical base64url), while the signing "
"input cannot. The payload binds the nonce, audience, ``iat`` and, through"
" ``sd_hash``, the EVT."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.replay_key:8
msgid ""
"A raw token is parsed first and raises :class:`~pyevp.TokenError` if "
"malformed."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verification_steps:1
msgid "Full RP verification.  Yields effects; returns :class:`VerifiedEmail`."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verification_steps:3
msgid ""
"Order matters: everything that can be checked offline (including the key-"
"binding signature) is checked before any network effect is requested, and"
" the only hosts ever contacted are derived from DNS, never from the "
"token. With ``replay_protection`` the token is marked as used once "
"everything else has passed, so that garbage tokens cannot fill the replay"
" store."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verify_evt_signature:1
msgid "Verify the EVT signature against an issuer JWK Set."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verify_evt_signature:3
msgid ""
"Raises ``KEY_NOT_FOUND`` when no key could even be tried, so the caller "
"may refresh the key set; ``EVT_SIGNATURE_INVALID`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verify_kb:1
msgid "Verify the key-binding JWT against the holder key bound in the EVT."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.core.verify_kb:3
msgid "Returns the KB-JWT's ``iat``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token:1
msgid "Presentation token codec: ``<EVT>~[<disclosure>~...]<KB-JWT>``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token:3
msgid ""
"Parsing only splits and decodes; it performs no signature checks.  The "
"build helpers are used by :mod:`pyevp.testing` and are kept here so a "
"future issuer implementation can reuse them."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token.CompactJWT:1
msgid "A compact JWS whose header and payload were decoded but not verified."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token.ParsedToken.sd_hash_input:1
msgid "Everything before the KB-JWT, including the trailing ``~``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token.build_kb:1
msgid "Append a key-binding JWT to an EVT, producing the presentation token."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token.build_kb:3
msgid ""
"``evt`` may carry the SD-JWT ``~`` that issuers append "
"(``issuance_token``) or not."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.token.sign_jwt:1
msgid ""
"Sign ``claims`` as a compact JWS.  ``private_key`` is a joserfc key "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery:1
msgid "Issuer discovery: pure functions, no I/O."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.canonical_issuer:1
msgid "Turn an issuer identifier into its ``https://host`` form."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.canonical_issuer:3
msgid ""
"Returns ``None`` when ``value`` is not acceptable under ``accepted``.  "
"The host is not case-folded: the drafts require byte-for-byte comparison."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.email_domain:1
msgid "Return the DNS (A-label) form of the domain part of ``email``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.email_domain:3
msgid ""
"Internationalised domains are mapped with UTS #46 / IDNA2008, as browsers"
" do. Python's ``\"idna\"`` codec implements IDNA2003, which maps some "
"names onto other domains (``faß.example`` → ``fass.example``).  Raises "
":class:`UnicodeError` for invalid internationalised domains."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.is_public_hostname:1
msgid "Whether ``host`` may name a public issuer host."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.is_public_hostname:3
msgid ""
"Rejects IP literals, single-label names and special-use names such as "
"``localhost``, so that a DNS record or metadata document chosen by an "
"attacker cannot point the verifier at the relying party's own network.  "
"The addresses a public name resolves to are checked by the HTTP adapters "
"before connecting."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.parse_txt_records:1
msgid "Extract the canonical issuer from the TXT records of the discovery name."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.discovery.validate_jwks:1
msgid ""
"Return the usable public keys of a JWK Set; unknown or private entries "
"are dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api.md:39
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics:1
msgid ""
"Issuer diagnostics: what a relying party sees when it discovers a "
"domain's issuer."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics:3
msgid ""
"Used by ``pyevp discover``, by the weekly drift check, and by issuer "
"operators who want to check their DNS record, metadata and keys against a"
" profile."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics.adiscover:1
msgid "Async counterpart of :func:`discover`."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics.discover:1
msgid "Run :func:`discovery_steps` with synchronous ports (no caching)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics.discovery_steps:1
msgid "Sans-I/O issuer check for an email address or domain."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.diagnostics.discovery_steps:3
msgid ""
"Content problems are collected in :attr:`IssuerReport.problems`; "
"transport failures surface as :class:`~pyevp.DiscoveryError` from the "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api.md:45
msgid "Adapters"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.dnspython:1
msgid "TXT resolvers backed by dnspython (``pip install pyevp[dns]``)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.dnspython.DnsPythonResolver:1
msgid "Synchronous resolver."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.dnspython.DnsPythonResolver:3
msgid ""
"With ``require_dnssec=True`` the answer must carry the AD flag, which is "
"only meaningful when the configured upstream resolver validates DNSSEC "
"and the path to it is trusted (e.g. a local validating resolver)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.dnspython.DnssecError:1
msgid "The answer was not marked authenticated (AD) by the resolver."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.httpx:1
msgid ""
"JSON fetchers backed by httpx2 or httpx (``pip install pyevp[httpx2]`` / "
"``pyevp[httpx]``)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.httpx:3
msgid ""
"httpx2 is used for default clients when it is installed; a client from "
"either library can be passed in explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.httpx.AsyncHttpxFetcher:1
msgid "Asynchronous counterpart of :class:`HttpxFetcher` (asyncio or trio)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.httpx.HttpxFetcher:1
msgid "Synchronous fetcher."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.httpx.HttpxFetcher:3
msgid ""
"Redirects are not followed, compressed responses are refused and bodies "
"are size-capped. Before each request the host is resolved and refused "
"unless every address is globally routable; pass "
"``require_global_addresses=False`` to reach an issuer on a private "
"network (local development) or when an egress proxy enforces that policy "
"and resolves names itself.  ``resolve_host`` replaces the system resolver"
" used for that check."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.doh:1
msgid ""
"TXT resolvers over DNS-over-HTTPS JSON APIs (``pip install "
"pyevp[httpx2]`` or ``pyevp[httpx]``)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.doh:3
msgid ""
"Useful where plain DNS is unavailable or untrusted (serverless platforms,"
" locked-down networks).  Only an HTTP client is needed; dnspython is not."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.doh:6
msgid ""
"``require_dnssec`` checks the resolver's ``AD`` flag, which only means "
"that the DoH provider validated the answer: you are trusting that "
"provider over TLS. Unsigned zones (gmail.com, for example) never pass "
"this check."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.doh:10
msgid ""
"If you already use ``dnspython[doh]``, an RFC 8484 resolver is also "
"possible::"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters._doh.DnssecError:1
msgid "The answer was not marked authenticated (AD) by the DoH provider."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters._doh.DohError:1
msgid "The DoH provider failed or answered with an error (e.g. SERVFAIL)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.doh.DohResolver:1
msgid ""
"Synchronous DoH TXT resolver (Google by default; pass "
"``endpoint=CLOUDFLARE`` etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters._doh.parse_txt_data:1
msgid "Decode a JSON-API TXT ``data`` value into one string."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters._doh.parse_txt_data:3
msgid ""
"Cloudflare returns presentation format: each character-string quoted, "
"with ``\\\"``, ``\\\\`` and ``\\DDD`` escapes, separated by spaces.  "
"Google returns the strings already joined and unquoted."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib:1
msgid "A JSON fetcher and a DoH TXT resolver using only the standard library."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib:3
msgid ""
"Nothing beyond pyevp's core dependencies is needed, which suits "
"applications that already pick their own HTTP stack and do not want httpx"
" or dnspython::"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib:11
msgid ""
"Both are synchronous; async applications should use the httpx adapters. "
"Like those, they never follow redirects, refuse compressed responses and "
"cap body sizes.  Proxies from the environment (``HTTPS_PROXY``) are "
"honoured as usual for urllib; pass ``handlers`` to configure proxies or "
"TLS differently::"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib.UrllibDohResolver:1
msgid ""
"Synchronous DoH TXT resolver (Google by default; pass ``CLOUDFLARE`` "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib.UrllibDohResolver:3
msgid ""
"``require_dnssec=True`` checks the provider's ``AD`` flag, so it means "
"trusting that provider over TLS; unsigned zones (gmail.com, for example) "
"never pass it."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib.UrllibFetcher:1
msgid "Synchronous :class:`~pyevp.JsonFetcher` built on :mod:`urllib.request`."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.adapters.urllib.UrllibFetcher:3
msgid ""
"Like :class:`~pyevp.adapters.httpx.HttpxFetcher`, it refuses hosts that "
"do not resolve exclusively to globally routable addresses unless "
"``require_global_addresses=False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api.md:58
msgid "Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django:1
msgid "Django integration (``pip install pyevp[django]``)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django:3
msgid ""
":class:`DjangoCache` / :class:`AsyncDjangoCache` share issuer metadata "
"and key sets between workers through Django's cache framework."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django:5
msgid ""
":class:`DjangoReplayGuard` / :class:`AsyncDjangoReplayGuard` remember "
"accepted tokens in a database table.  Add ``\"pyevp.contrib.django\"`` to"
" ``INSTALLED_APPS`` and run ``migrate`` to create it."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django:18
msgid ""
"Caches and databases are looked up on every call, so these can be created"
" at import time, before Django's settings are configured."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django:21
msgid "For running an issuer, see :mod:`pyevp.contrib.django.issuer`."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.AsyncDjangoCache:1
msgid ""
"An :class:`~pyevp.AsyncCache` using Django's async cache API (``aget`` / "
"``aset``)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.AsyncDjangoCache:3
msgid "Takes the same arguments as :class:`DjangoCache` and shares its entries."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.AsyncDjangoReplayGuard:1
msgid ":class:`DjangoReplayGuard` for :class:`~pyevp.AsyncVerifier`."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.AsyncDjangoReplayGuard:3
msgid "The database work runs in Django's thread for synchronous code."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoCache:1
msgid "A :class:`~pyevp.Cache` backed by one of Django's ``CACHES``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoCache:3
msgid ""
"Use a backend shared between workers (Redis, Memcached, database) for the"
" cache to help; ``locmem`` is per process like "
":class:`~pyevp.InMemoryCache`. An evicted entry is simply fetched again."
"  With :class:`~pyevp.AsyncVerifier`, use :class:`AsyncDjangoCache`, "
"which does not block the event loop."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoReplayGuard:1
msgid "A :class:`~pyevp.ReplayGuard` storing accepted tokens in the database."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoReplayGuard:3
msgid ""
"Each token is a row keyed by its digest until the token expires; a second"
" insert of the same key fails on the primary key, so concurrent workers "
"cannot both accept a token.  Unlike a cache, the table never evicts rows "
"early, and database errors propagate, so verification fails closed. "
"Expired rows are deleted as new tokens are recorded."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoReplayGuard:9
msgid ""
"Each record is committed immediately in its own transaction, so a later "
"rollback of the request cannot undo it.  Called inside a transaction on "
"the same database (``ATOMIC_REQUESTS``, ``transaction.atomic()``, or with"
" autocommit off) it raises ``RuntimeError`` instead; point ``using`` at a"
" second alias for the same database with ``ATOMIC_REQUESTS`` off and "
"autocommit on.  Django's ``TestCase`` transactions are exempt."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoReplayGuard:16
msgid ""
"Requires ``\"pyevp.contrib.django\"`` in ``INSTALLED_APPS`` and "
"``migrate``."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer:1
msgid "Running an EVP issuer in Django (experimental)."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer:3
msgid ""
":class:`IssuerSite` serves everything Chrome needs from an issuer, with "
"the logged-in Django user deciding which addresses get tokens::"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer:12
msgid ""
"Subclass it to choose the issuer per request "
"(:meth:`IssuerSite.get_issuer`) or the addresses a user may get tokens "
"for (:meth:`IssuerSite.user_emails`).  Each endpoint is also a view of "
"its own, for mounting it somewhere else::"
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer:18
msgid ""
"The session cookie must be ``SameSite=None; Secure``, because Chrome's "
"requests to the issuer are cross-site; a system check warns otherwise.  "
"Add :class:`LoginStatusMiddleware` so that Chrome knows when users are "
"signed in."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer.AccountsView:1
msgid "The FedCM accounts endpoint Chrome checks before asking for a token."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer.IssuanceView:1
msgid ""
"The issuer's ``issuance_endpoint``: an EVT for a user who controls the "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer.IssuanceView:3
msgid ""
"Exempt from CSRF protection and from ``ATOMIC_REQUESTS``; use a "
"synchronous replay guard such as "
":class:`~pyevp.contrib.django.DjangoReplayGuard`. Put per-IP rate "
"limiting in front of it."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer.IssuanceView.as_view:1
msgid "Main entry point for a request-response process."
msgstr ""

#: of pyevp.contrib.django.issuer.IssuerSite:1
